WEBVTT

00:00:09.888 --> 00:00:18.068
Assembly drawing = views + parts list + item balloons. Make the parts list in the assembly first: click “Bill of Materials”

00:00:18.068 --> 00:00:25.334
Index, Name and Quantity are enough. Select the “Description” and “File Name” columns and press Delete

00:00:25.334 --> 00:00:37.334
The BOM is a spreadsheet; double-click to see it: items 1–4, names, quantities. Change the parts and it updates on recompute

00:00:37.971 --> 00:00:48.748
Drawing: A3 landscape frame (the mechanism is 190 mm tall, fits at 1:1)

00:00:48.748 --> 00:00:58.174
Select the whole assembly, insert a view; click “Rotate right” to look from the side, where crank, rod and needle bar share one plane; OK

00:00:58.174 --> 00:01:08.681
Scale 1:1, position X = 130, Y = 160

00:01:08.681 --> 00:01:20.681
Parts list: select the BOM, menu “TechDraw → Views from other workbenches → Spreadsheet view”, place it above the title block

00:01:27.293 --> 00:01:39.293
Item balloons: select the view, click “Balloon”, click on a part, move the circle aside; numbered 1–4 as in the parts list

00:01:50.268 --> 00:02:02.268
Title block: “Slider-crank mechanism”, drawing LS-200 (practice), scale 1:1

00:02:27.399 --> 00:02:38.268
Export PDF: File → Export PDF, LS-200

00:02:38.268 --> 00:02:49.040
An assembly drawing shows how the parts fit together, what each is and how many. Change a part and the view and parts list follow on recompute
